{% doc %}
  Everyone on this thread besides the customer and ourselves.

  A colleague copied on the third email stays copied on the tenth reply,
  which is what the customer expects and what every mail client does by
  default.

  Three kinds of address are left out. The requester's own, because they
  are already the To. Any of the department's own, because copying
  ourselves on our own reply is how a mail loop starts. And anything
  blank.

  Takes the list so far rather than the ticket, because the two callers
  want different things from it. Inbound mail adds to what is there. An
  agent's reply replaces it, since the box they edited was prefilled with
  it and anything they took out, they took out on purpose.

  @param {array} [existing] - The list so far. Omit to replace rather than add
  @param {object} department - The department, whose own addresses are excluded
  @param {object} contact - The requester, whose own addresses are excluded
  @param {array} [incoming] - Addresses to add, from an email or an agent
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  assign excluded = ''
  if contact.email != blank
    assign excluded = excluded | append: ' <' | append: contact.email | downcase | append: '>'
  endif
  for address in contact.emails
    assign excluded = excluded | append: ' <' | append: address | downcase | append: '>'
  endfor
  if department.inbound_address != blank
    assign excluded = excluded | append: ' <' | append: department.inbound_address | downcase | append: '>'
  endif
  if department.from_address != blank
    assign excluded = excluded | append: ' <' | append: department.from_address | downcase | append: '>'
  endif

  comment
    One pass over what we had and then what arrived, so the order is the
    order people joined the conversation.
  endcomment
  assign candidates = []
  for address in existing
    assign candidates = candidates | array_add: address
  endfor
  for address in incoming
    assign candidates = candidates | array_add: address
  endfor

  assign kept = []
  assign seen = ''
  for candidate in candidates
    assign address = candidate | strip | downcase
    if address == blank
      continue
    endif
    assign token = '<' | append: address | append: '>'
    if excluded contains token
      continue
    endif
    if seen contains token
      continue
    endif
    assign seen = seen | append: ' ' | append: token
    assign kept = kept | array_add: address
  endfor

  return kept
%}
